    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #359\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch `bb/relay-237-notifications-v1-01-05-replace-the-not-thr_dvrfz8k3w8` pushed to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #237: replaces the minimal `notifications(id, kind, payload, created_at)` stub with a durable, closed-catalog, user-bound schema and a shared transaction-bound writer.\n\n- **Migration 0030**: drops the old stub table and splits it in two — `manifest_drift_findings` (keeps the old drift-check dedupe mechanism unchanged, since it has no user and uses out-of-catalog kinds) and a new `notifications` table (`user_id NOT NULL REFERENCES users`, closed `kind` catalog via `CHECK` — 5 active kinds + 4 reserved with no producer yet — `title`, `link_href`, `source_table`, `source_id`, `transition_instance`, `created_at`, `read_at`), with a unique dedup index on `(source_table, source_id, kind, transition_instance)` and a partial unread index on `(user_id) WHERE read_at IS NULL`.\n- **`notifications/notify.ts`**: shared `writeNotification` writer that runs on the caller's `PoolClient` (so it commits/rolls back with the caller's transaction), resolves a localized title via the #147 catalog resolver against the target user's locale, and dedupes with `ON CONFLICT ... DO NOTHING`.\n- **`scheduler/sweep.ts`**: wired as the reference producer for `heartbeat_error` at both exhausted-retry sites, using the firing queue job's own id as the transition instance.\n- Updated all remaining references to the old table (`findings.ts`, `driftCheck.ts`, `testDb.ts`, and the drift-finding tests) plus new test coverage (`notify.test.ts`, a new `scheduler.test.ts` case).\n\nOut of scope per the issue: wiring the writer into other producer sites (approval requests, agent-run errors, automation errors, mail sync errors), implementing the reserved observability/restore-check producers, and push delivery.\n\nVerified this session: full build (11 packages), unit tests (127/127), integration tests against real Postgres (815/815), e2e tests (5/5), lint, dependency-boundary check, and migration numbering — all green.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
